            <ArticleTitle>Alternate indications for varicocele repair: non-obstructive azoospermia, pain, androgen deficiency and progressive testicular dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1288-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2011.10.033</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Varicocele repair is indicated for infertile men with clinical varicoceles. Some men with scrotal pain, low testosterone, non-obstructive azoospermia, and who are at risk for testicular dysfunction may also benefit from varicocelectomy.</AbstractText>
